WEBVTT

00:03.860 --> 00:06.240
What? You're not coming to the estate, Gil?

00:06.470 --> 00:10.510
I wasn't invited, so I'll wait at the inn.

00:10.510 --> 00:14.290
Nobles and adventurers generally don't mix.

00:14.290 --> 00:16.730
Despite all they ask us to do?

00:17.570 --> 00:21.740
From their perspective, 
they're doing us a favor by giving us work.

00:22.880 --> 00:24.700
I don't like that.

00:24.700 --> 00:27.010
I shouldn't have come after all.

00:31.450 --> 00:35.940
I'm sure there will be lots you don't like,
 but try not to blow your lid.

00:37.000 --> 00:39.970
I'll do my best to stay positive.

00:40.670 --> 00:42.460
Well, good luck.

00:56.490 --> 01:04.830
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:15.150 --> 02:20.570
<b>Episode 12 "Confronting the Past"</b>

02:20.220 --> 02:21.380
This way.

02:24.920 --> 02:26.500
Have a seat and wait here.

02:30.340 --> 02:33.770
<i>It's so fancy, I'm hesitant 
to drink out of it.</i>

02:35.490 --> 02:38.770
You must be Angeline
 the Black-Haired Valkyrie.

02:41.250 --> 02:43.080
Not very sociable, are you?

02:43.080 --> 02:47.520
After I asked my father to 
honor you and everything.

02:49.140 --> 02:51.260
Who are you?

02:52.250 --> 02:55.270
H-How dare you speak to me like that!

02:57.590 --> 03:01.290
I'm from the countryside. Forgive me.

03:02.370 --> 03:05.700
Demon king slayer or not,
you're still just an adventurer.

03:05.700 --> 03:07.780
I can overlook a bit of impertinence.

03:09.200 --> 03:11.530
I appreciate it.

03:11.850 --> 03:14.530
I am Villard Estogal.

03:14.530 --> 03:16.290
I trust you've heard of me.

03:22.240 --> 03:27.070
So my name is known as far as
a backwater town like Orphen!

03:31.960 --> 03:34.490
Was the demon king strong?

03:34.490 --> 03:36.690
Yes, it was.

03:36.690 --> 03:42.980
Good. I'd be embarrassed if I had 
recommended we acknowledge some fool.

03:42.980 --> 03:44.700
Consider it an honor.

03:46.660 --> 03:50.230
This should improve my father's opinion of me.

03:50.230 --> 03:53.210
I won't let my brother bask in <i>all</i> his praise.

03:55.170 --> 03:58.670
So, when will the ceremony be?

03:58.670 --> 04:00.480
In three days' time.

04:01.110 --> 04:03.000
Three days, huh?

04:03.000 --> 04:05.580
Now then, you look rather filthy.

04:06.230 --> 04:08.480
You! Take care of her!

04:08.740 --> 04:11.040
Draw a bath and get her a nice dress.

04:11.040 --> 04:13.500
Teach her the bare minimum 
of etiquette, too.

04:13.500 --> 04:15.450
Don't embarrass me!

04:15.450 --> 04:16.660
Yes, milord.

04:16.970 --> 04:20.160
Try not to cause too much trouble.

04:23.070 --> 04:24.990
Nobles are not to be underestimated.

04:25.760 --> 04:28.260
Say, who is that guy anyway?

04:28.260 --> 04:30.780
What? You mean you don't know?

04:30.780 --> 04:32.790
I don't have the slightest clue.

04:32.790 --> 04:36.440
Lord Villard is the second son
 of the grand duke.

04:36.440 --> 04:38.500
Huh.

04:43.060 --> 04:50.010
Well, I doubt I'll ever have three 
people wash me at once again.

04:50.230 --> 04:51.990
She's so wonderfully slender!

04:51.990 --> 04:53.640
Her locks are beautiful, too.

04:53.640 --> 04:55.690
What hairstyle would suit her?

04:55.690 --> 04:57.520
Then there's the color of her dress!

04:57.990 --> 05:00.180
Perhaps purple for Ms. Angeline?

05:00.180 --> 05:01.900
Oh, no, beige would be better.

05:01.900 --> 05:04.700
In that case, how about this dress?

05:02.400 --> 05:04.160
I'm tired from the long trip.

05:04.160 --> 05:05.790
Can we do this tomorrow?

05:04.700 --> 05:05.790
Wonderful!

05:10.700 --> 05:12.800
Nobles are not to be underestimated.

05:14.070 --> 05:15.440
Come in.

05:18.600 --> 05:20.800
I've brought your dinner.

05:21.850 --> 05:23.800
I'm amazed you snuck in.

05:24.350 --> 05:27.940
Social events are a busy time 
with lots of extra people.

05:27.940 --> 05:29.810
The confusion makes it easy.

05:31.070 --> 05:34.380
So, why'd you slip in here?

05:34.380 --> 05:36.220
To gather intel.

05:36.220 --> 05:38.890
I smell something fishy.

05:39.710 --> 05:40.900
Really?

05:40.900 --> 05:45.980
The grand duke's sons, 
influential noble families,

05:45.980 --> 05:51.790
and even the crown prince of Rhodesia 
have been invited to this event.

05:52.250 --> 05:54.420
Are you saying it's special?

05:54.420 --> 05:55.350
Sure am.

05:56.350 --> 05:58.910
You're getting quite the welcome, Ange.

05:59.210 --> 06:01.590
Well, I don't care for it.

06:01.590 --> 06:04.920
They're going to make a big deal of me
 in front of all those people...

06:05.270 --> 06:10.940
The duke's second son, Villard, apparently 
put you forward when the crown prince

06:10.940 --> 06:14.050
asked if there would be a star of the show.

06:14.050 --> 06:18.510
He competes with his brother 
Fernand over everything.

06:18.760 --> 06:20.260
They don't get along?

06:20.260 --> 06:23.350
It's not that serious between them,

06:23.350 --> 06:28.120
but their relationship with their 
youngest brother isn't great.

06:29.740 --> 06:31.360
So there are three of them?

06:31.700 --> 06:33.590
And the youngest one...

06:35.290 --> 06:36.890
Who is it?

06:36.890 --> 06:38.770
It's me, it's me!

06:41.410 --> 06:43.890
I insist you open doors for me at once!

06:44.540 --> 06:45.890
Right...

06:45.890 --> 06:48.810
I present you the grand duke's daughter.

06:48.810 --> 06:51.370
I'm Liselotte. Nice to meet you.

06:52.490 --> 06:54.130
I'm Angeline.

06:54.390 --> 06:57.340
You there, I would like some tea.

06:57.340 --> 06:59.130
Yes, milady.

07:00.210 --> 07:03.130
You're supposed to be an 
amazing adventurer, right?

07:03.130 --> 07:05.140
You're the Black-Haired Valkyrie?

07:05.140 --> 07:07.650
Well, yes...

07:07.650 --> 07:11.450
I just love hearing adventuring stories!

07:11.450 --> 07:14.360
Tell me about yours, Ms. Angeline.

07:14.840 --> 07:19.180
<i>I used to ask my dad to tell me stories, too.</i>

07:19.980 --> 07:24.220
All right. What kind of story would 
you like to hear, uh, milady?

07:27.000 --> 07:30.700
Wow, you're incredible.

07:30.960 --> 07:34.530
You've done all kinds of things
even though you're a girl.

07:34.530 --> 07:35.180
Yeah.

07:36.210 --> 07:38.740
This has been fun. Thank you.

07:39.030 --> 07:42.720
Say, Ange, we're friends, aren't we?

07:42.720 --> 07:46.230
Yes. We're... friends.

07:46.230 --> 07:49.290
I've always wanted an adventurer friend!

07:49.290 --> 07:53.750
And since you're my friend,
 I'll show you my secret.

07:53.750 --> 07:56.200
What? Your secret?

08:02.830 --> 08:05.140
So they've even got a dungeon.

08:05.630 --> 08:07.620
Kasim, Kasim!

08:07.910 --> 08:10.200
I told you not to come here anymore.

08:11.020 --> 08:12.150
Humph!

08:12.150 --> 08:16.230
Should you be speaking to me like 
that when I brought you alcohol?

08:18.500 --> 08:20.970
You brought a friend with you today?

08:20.970 --> 08:24.290
Yes, this is Angeline the demon king slayer.

08:24.780 --> 08:28.770
Huh. So you're the Black-Haired 
Valkyrie I've heard about.

08:29.130 --> 08:33.520
This is Kasim. He used to be 
a really strong adventurer.

08:33.520 --> 08:35.230
That was a long time ago.

08:35.880 --> 08:37.530
What are you doing down here?

08:37.800 --> 08:39.970
I was caught dining and dashing.

08:39.970 --> 08:43.870
They threw me in here when I put up a fight.

08:49.390 --> 08:51.660
They've got nice liquor here.

08:51.660 --> 08:52.940
Sheesh!

08:53.480 --> 08:55.570
Don't be afraid.

08:56.420 --> 08:59.210
There'd be no point in fighting you.

09:01.250 --> 09:03.450
Don't you want to get out of here?

09:03.450 --> 09:06.520
You seem like a pretty powerful mage.

09:06.520 --> 09:10.190
Not really. I don't have 
anything to do on the outside.

09:10.190 --> 09:11.870
What a waste.

09:11.870 --> 09:13.190
What is?

09:13.190 --> 09:18.190
It's hard to say, but looking at you makes 
me feel like something's going to waste.

09:20.970 --> 09:24.180
You're right. I've wasted my life.

09:25.190 --> 09:28.460
Hey, you. You have friends, don't you?

09:29.750 --> 09:32.970
Take good care of them.

09:36.860 --> 09:40.090
Was that something only 
adventurers understand?

09:40.630 --> 09:42.230
Not exactly.

09:43.130 --> 09:46.030
I'm getting cold. Let's go, Lise.

09:50.350 --> 09:53.200
So much has been happening. I'm exhausted.

09:54.770 --> 09:58.260
<i>I wonder what Dad is up to...</i>

10:06.450 --> 10:08.940
I wonder if Ms. Ange is all right.

10:08.940 --> 10:12.120
I hope Gil is supporting her like she needs.

10:12.120 --> 10:13.620
Hello!

10:17.910 --> 10:18.830
What?

10:19.210 --> 10:21.720
Red hair and a peg leg?

10:22.520 --> 10:23.720
Could you be...

10:23.720 --> 10:27.520
Oh, excuse me. My name is Belgrieve.

10:27.520 --> 10:29.500
I'd like to see Angeline.

10:29.500 --> 10:31.720
Do you know where she is?

10:33.250 --> 10:34.580
You're...

10:35.000 --> 10:35.900
What?

10:35.900 --> 10:37.250
It's Mr. Bel!

10:37.250 --> 10:37.990
Huh?

10:39.320 --> 10:40.890
What brings you here?

10:40.890 --> 10:42.710
Good to see you again, Mr. Bel.

10:42.970 --> 10:45.330
It's good to see you two as well.

10:45.330 --> 10:48.200
Ange's not around. What're you doing here?

10:48.490 --> 10:49.290
What?

10:49.290 --> 10:51.970
I-I'm sorry!

10:53.740 --> 10:56.370
I see. She's being honored.

10:56.370 --> 10:58.580
I'm truly sorry.

10:59.570 --> 11:02.090
Please get up, Mr. Lionel.

11:02.900 --> 11:09.080
Your daughter does so much for us, 
but all I do is ruin her plans.

11:09.080 --> 11:10.810
That's life.

11:10.810 --> 11:14.480
People in high places have obligations.

11:15.230 --> 11:21.430
I'm glad she didn't skip the 
ceremony to return home.

11:21.430 --> 11:24.990
Thank you for telling her 
what she needed to hear.

11:25.390 --> 11:29.720
No... I haven't done anything 
to deserve your gratitude.

11:29.720 --> 11:34.110
I thought the guild master would be awesome,
 but he's completely worthless.

11:34.540 --> 11:35.860
Mary.

11:36.380 --> 11:37.560
Sorry.

11:37.560 --> 11:40.290
It's fine. It's true.

11:40.290 --> 11:44.800
Um, could you introduce us to the elf?

11:45.930 --> 11:48.340
Oh, right. This is—

11:48.340 --> 11:51.220
I'm Marguerite. Nice to meet you.

11:51.220 --> 11:53.310
Call me Mary.

11:53.600 --> 11:56.760
I'm Miriam. Call me Miri.

11:56.760 --> 11:59.970
I'm Anessa. People call me Ane, but...

11:59.970 --> 12:01.570
Call me whatever you'd like.

12:02.690 --> 12:05.640
Mary's here to sign on as an adventurer.

12:06.360 --> 12:09.970
In that case, Mary, let's get 
you registered over here.

12:09.970 --> 12:12.240
Sure. I'll be back.

12:12.240 --> 12:13.080
Okay.

12:17.890 --> 12:19.200
Mr. Belgrieve!

12:19.500 --> 12:20.390
Yes?

12:20.780 --> 12:26.070
I'm not sure you should be having your 
daughter look for a wife for you.

12:26.070 --> 12:26.920
What?

12:27.880 --> 12:30.640
I-I shouldn't have said anything.

12:30.640 --> 12:32.260
Forget I mentioned it.

12:33.160 --> 12:35.070
Look for a wife?

12:37.390 --> 12:38.660
Ange's, uh...

12:40.930 --> 12:42.490
What about her?

12:42.490 --> 12:46.100
Oh, that's right! There's someone 
we should introduce you to.

12:46.100 --> 12:47.460
Right, right!

12:49.180 --> 12:51.860
You're that girl. We met back in Bordeaux.

12:54.220 --> 12:56.570
Um, my name is Charlotte.

12:56.570 --> 12:59.300
Thank you for saving me then.

13:00.420 --> 13:04.880
Well, I'm glad to see
 you're all right. You look well.

13:10.170 --> 13:11.390
What's the matter?

13:14.840 --> 13:16.140
Uh...

13:16.490 --> 13:18.380
A lot has happened.

13:18.380 --> 13:22.630
It really has. We have so much to tell you.

13:22.630 --> 13:26.150
Though Ange might be cross if we did...

13:26.150 --> 13:30.540
No, I'm sure it's fine. Ange is Ange.

13:30.540 --> 13:33.150
Now, what's this about finding a wife?

13:33.150 --> 13:34.440
Um, excuse me.

13:34.910 --> 13:39.810
I don't mind if you don't mind, but perhaps 
you should take this elsewhere.

13:42.010 --> 13:43.770
Red hair and a peg leg...

13:44.210 --> 13:46.420
Is that Belgrieve the Red Ogre?

13:47.660 --> 13:50.600
Er, maybe we should take our leave.

13:52.430 --> 13:54.940
You're friends with Graham the Paladin?!

13:55.190 --> 13:58.590
Your family's grown rather big.

13:59.700 --> 14:00.820
That's true.

14:00.820 --> 14:04.320
That reminds me... 
What's this talk of finding a wife?

14:04.740 --> 14:06.200
Well, uh...

14:06.200 --> 14:09.440
I th-think you should ask Ange about that.

14:10.520 --> 14:12.190
What am I to do with that girl?

14:12.490 --> 14:15.720
Mr. Bel, are you not interested
 in getting hitched?

14:15.720 --> 14:16.880
Don't waste your time.

14:18.140 --> 14:21.450
Bel's heart already belongs to someone.

14:21.450 --> 14:22.590
What?!

14:23.740 --> 14:26.950
I keep telling you, it's not like that.

14:26.950 --> 14:29.580
Who, who, who?! Someone from Turnera?

14:29.580 --> 14:31.980
Someone from your adventuring days?

14:31.980 --> 14:34.990
Have you come to Orphen to find her?

14:34.990 --> 14:38.470
No, I'm here to track down
 some old companions.

14:38.770 --> 14:41.070
Old companions?

14:41.070 --> 14:43.480
Are they still adventuring?

14:43.730 --> 14:47.340
I'm not sure. I haven't seen 
them in more than twenty years.

14:47.340 --> 14:49.490
What are their names?

14:50.700 --> 14:53.930
There's Percival, who was a good swordsman.

14:53.930 --> 14:55.810
Kasim was a mage.

14:55.810 --> 14:58.750
And there was an elf lady named Satie.

14:59.170 --> 15:01.690
Percival and Kasim?

15:01.690 --> 15:04.260
They're both S-rank adventurers.

15:07.640 --> 15:13.140
Mr. Percival is also known 
as the High Sword King.

15:14.630 --> 15:21.140
Mr. Kasim has quit adventuring, but he's
 made quite a name for himself as a mage.

15:21.720 --> 15:23.870
They call him the Sky Shatterer.

15:24.830 --> 15:29.010
Of course. They well and truly 
were incredibly talented.

15:29.560 --> 15:31.270
Are they still in Orphen?

15:31.530 --> 15:35.650
No. They left a long time ago.

15:36.080 --> 15:40.470
Ms. Satie left town even before them.

15:40.470 --> 15:45.170
She ended her career at A-rank, 
and I haven't heard of her since.

15:45.590 --> 15:48.280
Were they not in the same party?

15:48.280 --> 15:53.530
No. By the time I knew them, 
they were working separately.

15:53.530 --> 15:55.280
I see.

15:57.240 --> 16:00.180
Thank you for telling me.

16:00.180 --> 16:04.180
I'm sorry I don't know where they are.

16:04.180 --> 16:08.420
It's fine. Just hearing about 
them is enough for me.

16:08.420 --> 16:12.080
I only just arrived, so I'll take 
my time gathering information.

16:12.080 --> 16:15.200
We'll help. Right, Miri?

16:15.980 --> 16:21.210
I've got it! This elf named 
Satie is Mr. Bel's sweetheart.

16:21.790 --> 16:23.200
Correct!

16:26.430 --> 16:28.160
There you are!

16:28.160 --> 16:30.470
You're Belgrieve the Red Ogre, aren't you?

16:30.470 --> 16:32.210
Glad to meet you.

16:33.630 --> 16:37.020
You don't have any manners, do you?

16:37.020 --> 16:41.410
My name is Dortos. We're friends of Ange's.

16:41.410 --> 16:44.320
It's good to meet you, Mr. Belgrieve.

16:45.140 --> 16:50.820
The honor is mine, Mr. Cheborg the 
Annihilator and Mr. Dortos the Silver.

16:51.900 --> 16:54.020
You know who I am?

16:55.390 --> 16:57.830
Er, did you need something?

16:58.070 --> 17:01.570
Ah, right, right! I want to duel the Red Ogre.

17:01.570 --> 17:02.710
What?

17:02.710 --> 17:04.830
I'd like to request a duel as well.

17:04.830 --> 17:09.350
Before I die, I want to behold the swordsman
who can brush aside Ange's blows.

17:09.350 --> 17:12.590
I'm really not that impressive.

17:14.680 --> 17:17.280
<i>Fighting two legendary adventurers?</i>

17:17.280 --> 17:19.760
<i>Nothing would make a man of the blade happier.</i>

17:20.720 --> 17:22.250
Very well.

17:22.250 --> 17:26.080
I'm not sure I'll live up to your 
expectations, but I accept.

17:33.990 --> 17:35.610
Are you ready?

17:44.280 --> 17:45.330
Begin!

18:16.480 --> 18:19.990
Not many men hold up so well against me.

18:21.580 --> 18:25.550
I can't believe a man of your skill
has kept himself a secret.

18:25.550 --> 18:28.400
Let's get a drink and 
you can tell me all about yourself.

18:28.400 --> 18:30.020
My treat.

18:30.020 --> 18:36.130
You should rest today so you can be in 
top form tomorrow for our duel.

18:37.410 --> 18:38.880
Go easy on me.

18:41.120 --> 18:46.010
I thought that idiot was exaggerating,
 but he's for real.

18:55.410 --> 18:58.050
You're stunning in that dress, milady.

18:58.920 --> 19:00.590
Don't startle me like that!

19:01.290 --> 19:03.070
You look pretty cute.

19:03.070 --> 19:04.480
R-Really?

19:04.880 --> 19:07.310
Do you think my dad would like it?

19:07.310 --> 19:09.080
He might even cry tears of joy.

19:09.080 --> 19:10.750
You mean it?

19:11.760 --> 19:16.540
Now, let's go for a walk to make sure 
you can handle yourself in that dress.

19:17.690 --> 19:19.670
I can walk just fine—

19:22.510 --> 19:25.680
You won't be able to move 
when you need to like this.

19:31.150 --> 19:33.950
Why do they make this dress 
so difficult to move around in?

19:36.750 --> 19:40.060
Where are you going, pretty lady?

19:41.300 --> 19:42.580
Nowhere in particular.

19:45.020 --> 19:48.000
How do you do, Lord Fernand?

19:49.360 --> 19:52.290
<i>So this is the grand duke's heir.</i>

19:52.290 --> 19:53.780
I don't recognize you,

19:53.780 --> 19:57.980
which is odd since I know all the 
beautiful people around here.

19:58.330 --> 20:01.810
Would you do me the pleasure
of telling me your name?

20:02.390 --> 20:04.620
It's Angeline.

20:04.620 --> 20:07.010
My, what a surprise.

20:07.010 --> 20:10.070
I didn't expect the demon king slayer 
to be such a beautiful woman.

20:11.860 --> 20:13.240
Allow me to escort you.

20:13.240 --> 20:15.710
Where were you headed?

20:15.710 --> 20:18.700
U-Um, I was going for a walk...

20:18.700 --> 20:20.400
The weather is pleasant today.

20:20.400 --> 20:23.850
We should tour the gardens, not the mansion.

20:28.320 --> 20:32.320
Anyway, inviting you was the right decision.

20:32.670 --> 20:36.560
Your beauty will brighten the ceremony.

20:36.560 --> 20:38.350
R-Right...

20:38.350 --> 20:40.460
Well, well, Brother.

20:40.920 --> 20:41.830
Good day.

20:42.910 --> 20:44.070
Who is the young lady?

20:44.630 --> 20:47.050
The guest of honor for the ball.

20:47.050 --> 20:49.000
I'm Angeline.

20:49.560 --> 20:53.040
Oh? So you're the Black-Haired Valkyrie.

20:53.040 --> 20:54.560
I am Francois.

20:54.850 --> 20:56.310
My brother.

20:56.310 --> 20:57.700
Nice to meet you.

21:03.190 --> 21:07.460
I'm sorry. He takes it upon himself
 to guard the grounds,

21:07.460 --> 21:10.090
so he regards everyone warily.

21:10.460 --> 21:13.340
No one suspicious has snuck in, have they?

21:13.640 --> 21:18.150
I'm not sure. There are many 
people coming and going.

21:18.150 --> 21:21.100
It wouldn't be odd if someone 
strange slipped in.

21:24.100 --> 21:26.820
Don't scare our guest.

21:26.820 --> 21:30.090
This won't earn you Father's praise.

21:31.090 --> 21:35.600
And perhaps <i>you</i> 
shouldn't chase so many skirts.

21:35.840 --> 21:37.890
Angeline or whatever your name is,

21:37.890 --> 21:41.450
don't get carried away just 
because you were invited.

21:41.450 --> 21:44.960
You may find yourself unexpectedly tripped up.

21:47.100 --> 21:49.370
<i>There's something wrong with all of them.</i>

21:49.370 --> 21:51.440
<i>Nobles are not to be underestimated.</i>

21:59.970 --> 22:02.660
A waste, huh?

